WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.118
Sometimes things do not share out evenly. What is left over is called the remainder.

00:07.568 --> 00:11.747
We have thirteen counters to share between four friends.

00:12.197 --> 00:18.467
Hand them out one at a time. Each friend gets three counters. That uses twelve.

00:18.917 --> 00:24.002
One counter is left over. We write that as three remainder one.

00:24.452 --> 00:31.209
We can check. Four times three is twelve, and twelve plus the remainder one makes thirteen.
